        "title": "Mythology - Comparative Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Mythology is the systematic study of **sacred narratives** — stories that a culture uses to explain the origin of the world, the nature of divinity, the structure of society, and what it means to be human. Every major civilization independently developed remarkably similar narrative patterns, which is the central puzzle that comparative mythology tries to solve."
